    "title": "A Greek temple — order in stone",
    "description": "Doric order, the oldest of the classical Greek styles. Six columns front the cella; their proportion (height : diameter ≈ 5:1) and the triglyph-metope frieze date this to ~500 BCE. The Parthenon's blueprint, scaled down.",
